          "file": "services/ops/orchestrator.py",
          "line": 58,
          "quote": "Never draft an operator that can restart containers without approval.",
          "found_by": "agent"
        }
      ],
      "what": "The rule that drafting a restart-capable operator needs approval is written only in the instructions. Nothing in the config or code enforces it.",
      "why": "A rule that only the model reads can be missed or argued around; a setting in config cannot.",
      "impact": "One misread instruction could let the orchestrator draft and run a restart-capable operator with no one approving it.",
      "fix": "In services/ops/orchestrator.py, make the draft call require approval in code (from draft(role) to draft(role, require_approval=True)) and keep the sentence as a reminder.",
      "decide": null,
      "enforcement": "stated",
      "confidence": "medium",
